{"abstract": [{"text": "VoiceOver is a screen reader that lets people experience your app\u2019s interface without needing to see the screen.", "type": "text"}], "hierarchy": {"paths": [["doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/technologies", "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/human-interface-guidelines", "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/technologies"]]}, "identifier": {"interfaceLanguage": "swift", "url": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/voiceover"}, "kind": "article", "legalNotices": {"copyright": "Copyright &copy; 2026 Apple Inc. All rights reserved.", "privacyPolicy": "https://www.apple.com/privacy/privacy-policy", "termsOfUse": "https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/terms/site.html"}, "metadata": {"availableLanguages": ["en-US", "zh-CN", "ja-JP", "ko-KR"], "customMetadata": {"alert-date": "2025-03-07", "alert-text": "New page.", "supported-platforms": "ios,ipados,macos,tvos,visionos,watchos"}, "images": [{"identifier": "voiceover.svg", "type": "icon"}, {"identifier": "technologies-voiceover-thumbnail.png", "type": "card"}], "role": "article", "title": "VoiceOver"}, "primaryContentSections": [{"content": [{"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "technologies-VoiceOver-intro.png", "type": "image"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"text": "By supporting VoiceOver, you help people who are blind or have low vision access information in your app and navigate its interface and content when they can\u2019t see the display.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"text": "VoiceOver is supported in apps and games built for Apple platforms. It\u2019s also supported in apps and games developed in Unity using ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/apple/unityplugins", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": ". For related guidance, see ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/accessibility", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": ".", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"anchor": "Descriptions", "level": 2, "text": "Descriptions", "type": "heading"}, {"inlineContent": [{"text": "You inform VoiceOver about your app\u2019s content by providing alternative text that explains your app\u2019s interface and the content it displays.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Provide alternative labels for all key interface elements.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " VoiceOver uses alternative labels (which aren\u2019t visible onscreen) to audibly describe your app\u2019s interface. System-provided controls have generic labels by default, but you should provide more descriptive labels that convey your app\u2019s functionality. Add labels to any custom elements your app defines. Be sure to keep your descriptions up-to-date as your app\u2019s interface and content change. For developer guidance, see ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/SwiftUI/View-Accessibility", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": ".", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Describe meaningful images.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " If you don\u2019t describe key images in your app\u2019s content, people can\u2019t use VoiceOver to fully experience them within your app. Because VoiceOver helps people understand the interface surrounding images too, such as nearby captions, describe only the information the image itself conveys.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Make charts and other infographics fully accessible.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " Provide a concise description of each infographic that explains what it conveys. If people can interact with the infographic to get more or different information, make these interactions available to people using VoiceOver, too. The accessibility APIs offer ways to represent custom interactive elements so that assistive technologies can help people use them. For guidance, see ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/charts", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": ".", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Exclude purely decorative images from VoiceOver.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " It\u2019s unnecessary to describe images that are decorative and don\u2019t convey useful or actionable information. Excluding these images shows respect for people\u2019s time and reduces cognitive load when they use VoiceOver. For developer guidance, see ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/SwiftUI/View/accessibilityHidden(_:)", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": ", ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/AppKit/NSAccessibility-c.protocol/accessibilityElement", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": ", and ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/UIKit/UIAccessibilityElement/isAccessibilityElement", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": ".", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"anchor": "Navigation", "level": 2, "text": "Navigation", "type": "heading"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Use titles and headings to help people navigate your information hierarchy.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " The title is the first information someone receives from an assistive technology when arriving on a page or screen in your app. Offer unique titles that succinctly describe each page\u2019s content and purpose. Likewise, use accurate section headings that help people build a mental model of each page\u2019s information hierarchy.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Specify how elements are grouped, ordered, or linked.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " Proximity, alignment, and other visible contextual cues help sighted people perceive the relationships between elements. Examine your app for places where relationships among elements are visual only. Then, describe these relationships to VoiceOver.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"text": "VoiceOver reads elements in the same order people read content in the their active language and locale. For example, in US English, this is top-to-bottom, left-to-right. In the ungrouped example below, VoiceOver describes each image before moving on to the captions. In the grouped example, VoiceOver describes each image with its respective caption.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"columns": [{"alignment": "leading", "content": [{"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "voiceover-incorrect-grouping.png", "metadata": {"abstract": [{"text": "Ungrouped related elements make it hard for VoiceOver to accurately describe the UI.", "type": "text"}], "deviceFrame": "iPhone16-top-half"}, "type": "image"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "crossout.png", "type": "image"}], "type": "paragraph"}], "size": 1}, {"alignment": "leading", "content": [{"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "voiceover-correct-grouping.png", "metadata": {"abstract": [{"text": "Grouped related elements help VoiceOver accurately describe the UI.", "type": "text"}], "deviceFrame": "iPhone16-top-half"}, "type": "image"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "checkmark.png", "type": "image"}], "type": "paragraph"}], "size": 1}], "numberOfColumns": 2, "type": "row"}, {"inlineContent": [{"text": "For developer guidance, see ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/ObjectiveC/NSObject-swift.class/shouldGroupAccessibilityChildren", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": ".", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Inform VoiceOver when visible content or layout changes occur.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " People may find an unexpected content or layout change confusing because it means their mental map of the content is no longer accurate. It\u2019s crucial to report visible changes so VoiceOver and other assistive technologies can help people update their understanding of the content. For developer guidance, see ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/Accessibility/AccessibilityNotification", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": ".", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Support the VoiceOver rotor when possible.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " People can use an interface element called the VoiceOver rotor to navigate a document or webpage by headings, links, and other content types. You can help people navigate content in your app by identifying these elements to the rotor. The rotor can also bring up the braille keyboard. For developer guidance, see ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/SwiftUI/AccessibilityRotorEntry", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": " (SwiftUI), ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/UIKit/UIAccessibilityCustomRotor", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": " (UIKit), and ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/AppKit/NSAccessibilityCustomRotor", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": " (AppKit).", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"anchor": "Platform-considerations", "level": 2, "text": "Platform considerations", "type": "heading"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "No additional considerations for iOS, iPadOS, macOS, tvOS, or watchOS.", "type": "text"}], "type": "emphasis"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"anchor": "visionOS", "level": 3, "text": "visionOS", "type": "heading"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Be mindful that custom gestures aren\u2019t always accessible.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " When VoiceOver is turned on in visionOS, apps and games that define custom gestures don\u2019t receive hand input by default. This ensures people can explore the interface using their voice, without an app responding to hand input at the same time. A person can opt out of this behavior by enabling Direct Gesture mode, which disables standard VoiceOver gestures and lets apps process hand input directly. For developer guidance, see ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/visionOS/improving-accessibility-support-in-your-app", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": ".", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"anchor": "Resources", "level": 2, "text": "Resources", "type": "heading"}, {"anchor": "Related", "level": 4, "text": "Related", "type": "heading"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/accessibility", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/inclusion", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"anchor": "Developer-documentation", "level": 4, "text": "Developer documentation", "type": "heading"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/Accessibility", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/Accessibility/voiceover", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/UIKit/supporting-voiceover-in-your-app", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"anchor": "Videos", "level": 4, "text": "Videos", "type": "heading"}, {"items": ["doc://com.apple.documentation/videos/play/wwdc2019/254", "doc://com.apple.documentation/videos/play/wwdc2021/10121", "doc://com.apple.documentation/videos/play/wwdc2020/10116"], "style": "compactGrid", "type": "links"}, {"anchor": "Change-log", "level": 2, "text": "Change log", "type": "heading"}, {"header": "row", "rows": [[[{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Date", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}], [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Changes", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}]], [[{"inlineContent": [{"text": "March 7, 2025", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}], [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "New page.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}]]], "type": "table"}], "kind": "content"}], "schemaVersion": {"major": 0, "minor": 3, "patch": 0}, "sections": [], "topicSectionsStyle": "compactGrid", "references": {"1A6C1BBD-8ADD-4B35-896E-7EBAA39B82FC": {"alt": null, "identifier": "1A6C1BBD-8ADD-4B35-896E-7EBAA39B82FC", "type": "image", "variants": [{"traits": ["1x"], "url": "https://devimages-cdn.apple.com/wwdc-services/images/119/1A6C1BBD-8ADD-4B35-896E-7EBAA39B82FC/5019_wide_250x141_1x.jpg"}, {"traits": ["2x"], "url": "https://devimages-cdn.apple.com/wwdc-services/images/119/1A6C1BBD-8ADD-4B35-896E-7EBAA39B82FC/5019_wide_250x141_2x.jpg"}, {"traits": ["3x"], "url": "https://devimages-cdn.apple.com/wwdc-services/images/119/1A6C1BBD-8ADD-4B35-896E-7EBAA39B82FC/5019_wide_250x141_3x.jpg"}]}, "23AF104C-7CFE-4F7B-AEC6-46F54121AE92": {"alt": null, "identifier": "23AF104C-7CFE-4F7B-AEC6-46F54121AE92", "type": "image", "variants": [{"traits": ["1x"], "url": "https://devimages-cdn.apple.com/wwdc-services/images/48/23AF104C-7CFE-4F7B-AEC6-46F54121AE92/2966_wide_250x141_1x.jpg"}, {"traits": ["2x"], "url": "https://devimages-cdn.apple.com/wwdc-services/images/48/23AF104C-7CFE-4F7B-AEC6-46F54121AE92/2966_wide_250x141_2x.jpg"}, {"traits": ["3x"], "url": "https://devimages-cdn.apple.com/wwdc-services/images/48/23AF104C-7CFE-4F7B-AEC6-46F54121AE92/2966_wide_250x141_3x.jpg"}]}, "669BA7EE-2BAE-4B94-84E7-41D399756313": {"alt": null, "identifier": "669BA7EE-2BAE-4B94-84E7-41D399756313", "type": "image", "variants": [{"traits": ["1x"], "url": "https://devimages-cdn.apple.com/wwdc-services/images/49/669BA7EE-2BAE-4B94-84E7-41D399756313/3471_wide_250x141_1x.jpg"}, {"traits": ["2x"], "url": "https://devimages-cdn.apple.com/wwdc-services/images/49/669BA7EE-2BAE-4B94-84E7-41D399756313/3471_wide_250x141_2x.jpg"}, {"traits": ["3x"], "url": "https://devimages-cdn.apple.com/wwdc-services/images/49/669BA7EE-2BAE-4B94-84E7-41D399756313/3471_wide_250x141_3x.jpg"}]}, "Accessibility-PageImage-card.png": {"alt": "An illustration that shows three people: someone with low vision walking with the assistance of a guide dog while using an iPhone and AirPods; a person in a wheelchair using an iPhone; and a person wearing a hearing aid and a camping backpack while walking and using an iPhone.", "identifier": "Accessibility-PageImage-card.png", "type": "image", "variants": [{"traits": ["2x", "light"], "url": "/images/com.apple.Accessibility/Accessibility-PageImage-card@2x.png"}, {"traits": ["2x", "dark"], "url": "/images/com.apple.Accessibility/Accessibility-PageImage-card~dark@2x.png"}]}, "accessibility.svg": {"alt": "The Accessibility icon.", "identifier": "accessibility.svg", "type": "image", "variants": [{"svgID": "accessibility", "traits": ["1x", "light"], "url": "/images/com.apple.HIG/accessibility.svg"}]}, "checkmark.png": {"alt": "A checkmark in a circle to indicate correct usage.", "identifier": "checkmark.png", "type": "image", "variants": [{"traits": ["2x", "light"], "url": "/images/com.apple.HIG/checkmark@2x.png"}]}, "components-charts-thumbnail.png": {"alt": "A stylized representation of a bar chart. The image is tinted red to subtly reflect the red in the original six-color Apple logo.", "identifier": "components-charts-thumbnail.